<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sudarshana Lake</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sudarshana Lake was an ancient reservoir near Junagadh in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, built under the Maurya emperor Chandragupta by his governor Pushyagupta and improved under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a>. Its history is recorded in inscriptions on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girnar">Girnar</a> rock: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudradaman-i">Rudradaman I</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-satraps">Western Satraps</a> repaired it after a storm breached the dam in the 2nd century CE, and a governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skandagupta">Skandagupta</a> restored it again in 456. Its exact site is no longer certain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sudarshana-lake.jpg" alt="Sudarshana Lake" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Prashantsangani · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_on_Girnar_Taleti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
